{
  "result": "If I had one wish and one wish only - I'd give everyone real, lived empathy.\n\nNot the polite idea of empathy where we say \"I understand,\" but the real thing. Like for two minutes a day, you involuntarily feel what someone else is feeling. The anxiety of the single mom in line behind you at the grocery store. The exhausted pride of the farmer who grew your coffee. The loneliness of the teenager who seems like he's trying to be rude.\n\nI wouldn't make everyone agree with each other. I wouldn't erase disagreement or debate or different values. But you couldn't dehumanize someone if you'd felt what it's like to *be* them for even a moment.\n\nI think almost everything else we want to fix - war, cruelty, poverty, polarization, even how we treat the planet - comes from a failure of imagination. We literally can't imagine what it's like to be the other person, or the future generation who has to live with our choices.\n\nIf people could genuinely feel each other, I think we'd still argue, but we wouldn't be cruel about it. We'd still have borders and different beliefs, but we wouldn't be able to tolerate letting a child go hungry anywhere. We'd still want to succeed, but not by destroying each other to do it.\n\nIt fixes the root, not just the symptoms.\n\nWhat would yours be?",
